  "foaf:name": "Oslofjord kelp park",
  "sdo:name": "Oslofjord kelp park",
  "sdo:description": "Oslofjord Kelp Park is a nature-based pilot project demonstrating how sustainable kelp cultivation can support ecological restoration, nutrient reduction, carbon sequestration, and blue bioeconomy development in the Oslofjord, Norway. The project addresses eutrophication, biodiversity loss, and declining water quality through nature-based solutions. Kelp absorbs excess nitrogen and phosphorus, binds CO₂, produces oxygen, creates habitat structure, and enhances biodiversity, functioning as a natural water purification system. A core element is a dedicated research program assessing the real, measurable effects of the kelp facility. The research will identify which ecosystem services are delivered such as nutrient uptake, carbon sequestration, biodiversity enhancement, and water quality improvements and evaluate whether and how these services can be quantified.",
  "sdo:location": "Norway",
  "sdo:identifier": "48.1",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/oslofjord-kelp-park/",
